{#
  User avatar — the member's photo when there is one, their initials when there is not.

  🔴 This partial rendered initials ONLY, with no <img> in it at all, which is why the
  member profile page never showed a photo while the members directory did: the directory
  writes its own <img> inline. Anything using this partial was silently initials-only.

  Parameters:
    - user: object with first_name/firstName, last_name/lastName, and an avatar field
    - size: 'small' (32px), 'large' (64px), or omit for the 40px default

  The photo is requested from the API at twice its displayed size so it stays sharp on a
  high-density screen while still being a few kilobytes rather than the full upload — see
  the `thumb` filter in src/lib/template-filters.js.

  width/height are set on the element as well as in CSS. That is deliberate: it lets the
  browser reserve the right space before the stylesheet arrives, so the page does not jump
  as avatars load. It matters more on this frontend than most, because its audience skews
  towards slow connections and assistive technology, where reflow is disorienting.

  alt is empty because every use of this partial sits directly beside the member's name in
  text. A screen reader announcing the name twice is worse than not describing a decorative
  photo — where an avatar stands alone without a visible name, write markup with a real alt
  instead of using this partial.
#}
{% set firstName = (user.first_name or user.firstName or '') | string %}
{% set lastName = (user.last_name or user.lastName or '') | string %}
{% set firstInitial = firstName[0] if firstName.length > 0 else '' %}
{% set lastInitial = lastName[0] if lastName.length > 0 else '' %}
{% set initials = firstInitial + lastInitial %}
{% set fullName = firstName + ' ' + lastName %}

{% set avatarSource = user.avatarUrl or user.avatar_url or user.avatar or user.profile_image or '' %}
{% set avatarPx = 32 if size == 'small' else (64 if size == 'large' else 40) %}

{% if avatarSource %}
  <img class="app-avatar{% if size %} app-avatar--{{ size }}{% endif %} app-avatar--image"
       src="{{ avatarSource | thumb(avatarPx * 2, avatarPx * 2) }}"
       width="{{ avatarPx }}" height="{{ avatarPx }}"
       alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
{% else %}
  <span class="app-avatar{% if size %} app-avatar--{{ size }}{% endif %}" aria-hidden="true" title="{{ fullName | trim }}">
    {{ initials | upper if initials else '?' }}
  </span>
{% endif %}
